From 3cc062ad68d9430e3ca79d0e32281cff933e33b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:25:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/rknpu: legacy /dev/rknpu surface on the DRM GEM
 backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The vendor kernel only registers the legacy misc device together with the
DMA_HEAP memory manager (vendor heap framework, absent on mainline); the
misc open is what selects librknnrt's legacy 'r'-ioctl path (dsh-006
mode 0, RE evidence .claude/rknn/dyn/run7.log). Without it the runtime
falls back to the DRM path — a surface our byte-exact engine does not
speak.

rknpu_legacy.c wires the legacy contract onto GEM:
- ACTION/SUBMIT share the same cores as the DRM path (rknpu_action /
  rknpu_submit, now non-static)
- MEM_CREATE = rknpu_gem_object_create + prime export; handle field
  carries the dma-buf fd (matches the RE'd contract), obj_addr/dma_addr
  filled like the GEM create ioctl
- MEM_SYNC reuses rknpu_gem_sync_ioctl (it addresses by obj_addr)
- MEM_DESTROY drops the session-tracked reference after obj_addr
  validation; MEM_MAP is -ENOTTY (legacy blob path never uses it)

miscdev member moves out of the DMA_HEAP ifdef; rknpu_legacy_register()
is called from probe after rknpu_drm_probe().
---
 drivers/rknpu/Makefile               |   2 +-
 drivers/rknpu/include/rknpu_drv.h    |   5 +-
 drivers/rknpu/include/rknpu_job.h    |   2 +
 drivers/rknpu/include/rknpu_legacy.h |  10 ++
 drivers/rknpu/rknpu_drv.c            |  17 +-
 drivers/rknpu/rknpu_gem.c            |   1 -
 drivers/rknpu/rknpu_job.c            |   2 +-
 drivers/rknpu/rknpu_legacy.c         | 243 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 8 files changed, 273 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/rknpu/include/rknpu_legacy.h
 create mode 100644 drivers/rknpu/rknpu_legacy.c

